   "widgets_values": [
    "{\"v\": 1, \"title\": \"Qwen Image 2.1 Edit + Realign\", \"subtitle\": \"Type a short edit. Qwen Image 2.1 makes it, and Realign to Source lines it back up with your picture.\", \"author\": \"AusBoss\", \"layout\": \"card\", \"accent\": \"#8fa8c8\", \"body\": \"## Start here\\nCopy `ausboss_pier_sunrise.png` from the pack's `example_workflows/inputs/` folder into `ComfyUI/input/`, or choose your own picture. Select the three downloaded models, type your change in **Your edit**, and queue.\\n\\n## What each part does\\n1. **Image Resize** makes your picture about 1 MP. **Margin**, a Load Image + Pad, adds 64 px of mirrored picture on every side, so the edit has room to move. The wire into its `source_image` wins over its file row.\\n2. **Prompt writer**: Qwen3-VL 8B, the same text encoder the edit uses, looks at your picture and turns your short edit into a full instruction. **Rewritten instruction** shows what it wrote. Change **Writer instructions** to taste.\\n3. **Encode + sample**: Qwen Image 2.1 makes the edit. Keep the encoder's `latent` on the sampler: a canvas of another size adds a zoom of its own.\\n4. **Realign to Source** lines the edit back up with your picture and cuts the margin off. **Report** says how far the edit had moved.\\n5. **Before** and **After** slide the edit against your picture, and **Save Image** writes the result with this workflow inside.\\n\\n## Why realign\\nQwen Image 2.1 often draws a style edit slightly bigger or shifted, by a different amount every seed. With this seed the watercolor came back 2.6% taller and 9 px lower, about 25 px off at the worst corner. Realign to Source moved it back, and thanks to the margin there are no empty edges.\\n\\n## Tips\\n- Moving a person's arm or hand? Say where it ends up and what changes, like `put her arm on the table, her hands aren't clasped anymore`. Otherwise Qwen tends to keep the old pose and add a new arm.\\n- To skip the writer, wire **Your edit** straight into the encoder's `prompt`.\\n- The [Qwen Image 2.1 Consistency LoRA](https://huggingface.co/ausboss/Qwen-Image-2.1-Consistency-LoRA) keeps edits in place by itself. Load it with a LoRA Loader between the diffusion model and the reference cache, as the Qwen Image 2.1 Edit example does, and set the Margin's four pads to 0.\\n- Realign to Source is experimental. It fixes the whole picture moving, not things the edit redrew in a new spot. If the report names a side and pixels, the edit ran past the margin there: raise that pad, or try another seed.\\n\\n## Sampling\\n25 steps, CFG 1, Euler / simple, denoise 1, with a fixed seed. The margin adds about 27% more pixels to render.\\n\\n## Models\\nEach Download button below names its destination under `ComfyUI/models/`. Refresh the model list after copying files. The model repository also provides optional BF16 alternatives.\", \"models\": [{\"name\": \"qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors\", \"dir\": \"diffusion_models\", \"size\": \"7.26 GB\", \"note\": \"Selected INT8 diffusion model.\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors\"}, {\"name\": \"qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors\", \"dir\": \"text_encoders\", \"size\": \"9.35 GB\", \"note\": \"Selected Qwen3-VL 8B encoder; CLIP type: qwen_image.\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors\"}, {\"name\": \"qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors\", \"dir\": \"vae\", \"size\": \"676 MB\", \"note\": \"Use the Qwen Image 2.1 VAE.\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors\"}], \"packs\": [], \"links\": [{\"label\": \"Qwen 2.1 model files + BF16 alternatives\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1\"}, {\"label\": \"Qwen model guide\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1\"}]}",
    ""
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "note": "{\"v\": 1, \"title\": \"Qwen Image 2.1 Edit + Realign\", \"subtitle\": \"Type a short edit. Qwen Image 2.1 makes it, and Realign to Source lines it back up with your picture.\", \"author\": \"AusBoss\", \"layout\": \"card\", \"accent\": \"#8fa8c8\", \"body\": \"## Start here\\nCopy `ausboss_pier_sunrise.png` from the pack's `example_workflows/inputs/` folder into `ComfyUI/input/`, or choose your own picture. Select the three downloaded models, type your change in **Your edit**, and queue.\\n\\n## What each part does\\n1. **Image Resize** makes your picture about 1 MP. **Margin**, a Load Image + Pad, adds 64 px of mirrored picture on every side, so the edit has room to move. The wire into its `source_image` wins over its file row.\\n2. **Prompt writer**: Qwen3-VL 8B, the same text encoder the edit uses, looks at your picture and turns your short edit into a full instruction. **Rewritten instruction** shows what it wrote. Change **Writer instructions** to taste.\\n3. **Encode + sample**: Qwen Image 2.1 makes the edit. Keep the encoder's `latent` on the sampler: a canvas of another size adds a zoom of its own.\\n4. **Realign to Source** lines the edit back up with your picture and cuts the margin off. **Report** says how far the edit had moved.\\n5. **Before** and **After** slide the edit against your picture, and **Save Image** writes the result with this workflow inside.\\n\\n## Why realign\\nQwen Image 2.1 often draws a style edit slightly bigger or shifted, by a different amount every seed. With this seed the watercolor came back 2.6% taller and 9 px lower, about 25 px off at the worst corner. Realign to Source moved it back, and thanks to the margin there are no empty edges.\\n\\n## Tips\\n- Moving a person's arm or hand? Say where it ends up and what changes, like `put her arm on the table, her hands aren't clasped anymore`. Otherwise Qwen tends to keep the old pose and add a new arm.\\n- To skip the writer, wire **Your edit** straight into the encoder's `prompt`.\\n- The [Qwen Image 2.1 Consistency LoRA](https://huggingface.co/ausboss/Qwen-Image-2.1-Consistency-LoRA) keeps edits in place by itself. Load it with a LoRA Loader between the diffusion model and the reference cache, as the Qwen Image 2.1 Edit example does, and set the Margin's four pads to 0.\\n- Realign to Source is experimental. It fixes the whole picture moving, not things the edit redrew in a new spot. If the report names a side and pixels, the edit ran past the margin there: raise that pad, or try another seed.\\n\\n## Sampling\\n25 steps, CFG 1, Euler / simple, denoise 1, with a fixed seed. The margin adds about 27% more pixels to render.\\n\\n## Models\\nEach Download button below names its destination under `ComfyUI/models/`. Refresh the model list after copying files. The model repository also provides optional BF16 alternatives.\", \"models\": [{\"name\": \"qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors\", \"dir\": \"diffusion_models\", \"size\": \"7.26 GB\", \"note\": \"Selected INT8 diffusion model.\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors\"}, {\"name\": \"qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors\", \"dir\": \"text_encoders\", \"size\": \"9.35 GB\", \"note\": \"Selected Qwen3-VL 8B encoder; CLIP type: qwen_image.\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors\"}, {\"name\": \"qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors\", \"dir\": \"vae\", \"size\": \"676 MB\", \"note\": \"Use the Qwen Image 2.1 VAE.\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors\"}], \"packs\": [], \"links\": [{\"label\": \"Qwen 2.1 model files + BF16 alternatives\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1\"}, {\"label\": \"Qwen model guide\", \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1\"}]}",
    "ausboss_workflow_note_panel": ""
